{title: 434 - We Speak of the Realms}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #434 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 434}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/A]We speak of [Am]the realms of the blest,
[F]That country so [Bb/F]bright and [F]so fair,
[Gm]And oft are [Am]its glories [C]confessed-
[Dm/A]But what must [Am]it be to be there!
[F]We speak [Gm/D]of [C7]its [Am]pathway [C]of [Am]gold-
[Am]Its walls decked [F]with jewels so rare,
[Am]Its wonders and pleasures [F]untold-
[Gm]But what must [Am]it be to [C]be there!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/A]We speak of [Am]its freedom of sin,
[F]From sorrow, temptation and care,
[Gm]From trials without [Am]and [C]within---
[Dm/A]But what must [Am]it be to be there!
[F]We speak [Gm/D]of [C7]its [Am]service [C]of [Am]love,
[Am]Of the robes [F]which glorified wear,
[Am]Of the church of the [Bb/F]First Born [F]above-
[Gm]But what must [Am]it be to [C]be there!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/A]Our mourning [Am]is all at an end,
[F]When, raised by the life-giving word,
[Gm]We see the [Am]new city [C]descend,
[Dm/A]Adorned as [Am]a bride for her Lord;
[F]The city [C7]so [Am]holy [C]and [Am]clean,
[Am]No sorrow [F]can breathe in the air;
[Am]No gloom of affliction [F]or sin,
[Gm]No shadow [Am]of evil, [C]is there.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm/A]Do Thou, midst [Am]temptation and woe,
[F]For heaven my [Bb/F]spirit [F]prepare;
[Gm]And shortly [Am]I also [C]so shall know
[Dm/A]And feel what [Am]it is to be there.
[F]Then o'er [Gm/D]the [C7]bright [Am]fields [C]we shall [Am]roam,
[Am]In glory [F]celestial and fair,
[Am]With saints and with [Bb/F]angels [F]at home,
[Gm]And Jesus [Am]Himself will [C]be there.
{end_of_verse}
